{
  title: "138 window, window-all, partition and partition-all"
  doc: "Sliding windows and partitions over lists. eu-oaz72.49 made a step
        that is not positive an error for `window` and `window-all`, and a
        size that is not positive an error for `window` (see
        tests/harness/errors/235_oaz72_49_*.eu); `window-all` with a size
        that is not positive still gives []. eu-oaz72.56 made `window-all`
        and `partition-all` linear and lazy (they counted the remaining
        list at every step), and let `window` take a step past the end of
        the list (it failed in `drop`)."
}

` "every check in the target is true"
passes(context): (context.result values all-true?) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :window-checks
    verify: [:passes] }
window-checks: {
  step-1: ([1, 2, 3, 4] window(2, 1)) = [[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4]]
  step-2: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] window(2, 2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
  step-gt-size: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] window(2, 3)) = [[1, 2], [4, 5]]
  step-past-end: ([1, 2, 3] window(2, 5)) = [[1, 2]]
  short: ([1] window(2, 1)) nil?
  infinite: (ints-from(0) window(3, 2) take(2)) = [[0, 1, 2], [2, 3, 4]]
  partition-even: ([1, 2, 3, 4] partition(2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
  over-sliding-pairs-ok: ([1, 3, 6] over-sliding-pairs(-)) = [-2, -3]
}

` { target: :window-all-checks
    verify: [:passes] }
window-all-checks: {
  step-1: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(2, 1)) = [[1, 2], [2, 3], [3]]
  step-2: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] window-all(2, 2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5]]
  overlapping: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] window-all(3, 2)) = [[1, 2, 3], [3, 4, 5], [5]]
  sliding: ([1, 2, 3, 4] window-all(3, 1)) = [[1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4], [3, 4], [4]]
  step-gap: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] window-all(2, 3)) = [[1, 2], [4, 5]]
  step-past-end: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(2, 5)) = [[1, 2]]
  empty: ([] window-all(2, 1)) nil?
  size-zero: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(0, 1)) nil?
  size-negative: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(-1, 1)) nil?
  size-zero-step-zero: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(0, 0)) nil?
  size-negative-step-zero: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(-1, 0)) nil?
}

` { target: :partition-all-checks
    verify: [:passes] }
partition-all-checks: {
  short-tail: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] partition-all(2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5]]
  exact: ([1, 2, 3, 4] partition-all(2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
  larger: ([1, 2] partition-all(3)) = [[1, 2]]
  empty: ([] partition-all(2)) nil?
  zero: ([1, 2, 3] partition-all(0)) nil?
  negative: ([1, 2, 3] partition-all(-2)) nil?
}

` "A long finite list standing in for an infinite one, so a regression FAILs on the tick budget instead of hanging."
long: range(0, 1000000)

` "taking a few windows does not walk the list"
few-ticks(context): (context.stats.ticks < 100000) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :lazy
    verify: [:passes, :few-ticks]
    doc: "eu-oaz72.56: the old `window-all` counted the whole remaining list
          before yielding each window, so on an infinite list it never
          returned. Taking a few windows must cost nothing like the length
          of the list." }
lazy: {
  wa: (long window-all(2, 1) take(3)) = [[0, 1], [1, 2], [2, 3]]
  pa: (long partition-all(3) take(2)) = [[0, 1, 2], [3, 4, 5]]
  w: (long window(2, 3) take(2)) = [[0, 1], [3, 4]]
}

` "List length for the cost target: the linear version is far inside the budget, the quadratic one far outside it."
n: 4000

` "the cost is linear in the length of the list"
linear-cost(context): (context.stats.ticks < 1000 * n) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :cost
    verify: [:passes, :linear-cost]
    doc: "eu-oaz72.56: one `count` per window over the remaining list made
          `window-all` quadratic; the tick budget is per element." }
cost: {
  pa: (range(0, n) partition-all(2) count) = n / 2
  wa: (range(0, n) window-all(2, 1) count) = n
}
